{
  "standing": "SYNTHETIC schedules evaluated by security_lifecycle_model_v1.revocation_observe, .observer_tick, .linearize, .admit_journal_record and .admit_host_seal_run_id (AR-05). `schedule` is the order in which actors acquire the journal append lock L. Linearization covers BROKERED effects only: no brokered effect commits after REV; a reversible completed effect is rolled back only when its current bytes equal the committed postimage (EDIT models a user change since commit; INDET an unreadable target); unconfined children (CHILD) are cancelled within the bound and disclosed, their external effects are not enumerable. Current journal records are recordSchema 3 with run3; schema-2 journals are frozen historical bytes and are not read as 3. The all-zero SEAL runId is a linearization fixture, not native or evaluator authority. Observer bounds are implementation qualification obligations under OS scheduling assumptions. Expected values were authored by hand from security-and-lifecycle.md S6 before execution (same author, not an independent oracle). No process was spawned or killed.",
